                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "178143e7-0683-3941-b32b-e347bc280081",
                        "entry_id": "5c9e337e-e406-3b76-a59c-75427f3096b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "единица измерения мощности электрического тока, равная 1000 ватт"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0337aa56-9190-40e9-a0b3-c4c601de3942",
                                "sense_id": "178143e7-0683-3941-b32b-e347bc280081",
                                "text": "Берегите электричество, // Чтобы каждый киловатт // Увеличивал количество // Пушек, танков и гранат."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4a022f7-a4fd-4ef3-a651-28b0bcf434a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c9e337e-e406-3b76-a59c-75427f3096b7",
                        "source_sense_id": "178143e7-0683-3941-b32b-e347bc280081",
                        "target_lang_word": "kilowatt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kilowatt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81297f9a-3722-37c5-a35d-125d285fb397",
                                        "entry_id": "b528b133-4a9d-3a45-9e61-57d9a5003d46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One thousand (10³) watts, an amount of power large enough to power such things as a typical home appliance (e.g., a microwave oven, a toaster, or a hair dryer). (Consuming 1 kilowatt during a duration of 1 hour consumes 1 kilowatt-hour of energy.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eab3e2e7-cf34-4dec-a878-519b0b66dabc",
                                                "sense_id": "81297f9a-3722-37c5-a35d-125d285fb397",
                                                "text": "Holonyms: MW, megawatt < GW, gigawatt < TW, terawatt < PW, petawatt"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d980d7-561c-4da0-82d7-344d595d68cd",
                                                "sense_id": "81297f9a-3722-37c5-a35d-125d285fb397",
                                                "text": "Meronyms: mW, milliwatt < W, watt"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6308c93-60fc-4c36-b619-109049f640bd",
                                                "sense_id": "81297f9a-3722-37c5-a35d-125d285fb397",
                                                "text": "And one California kilowatt equals 3 East Coast KWs. And—as everybody knows that—we, on the East Coast, are the only legal ones."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61d4fc12-bbca-4b9e-8000-3f538df4beec",
                                                "sense_id": "81297f9a-3722-37c5-a35d-125d285fb397",
                                                "text": "Each turbogenerator consisted of a steam turbine, powered by 900 psi of superheated steam, that was coupled by a set of reduction gears to a General Electric marine alternating-current generator operating at 1,800 rpm. Each generator had a capacity of 2,000 kilowatts of three-phase power at 450 volts and 60 hertz. The main 450-volt switchboard was energized by the two turbogenerators. The emergency switchboard, in the emergency generator room, was fed from the main switchboard through an electrical tie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57156653-2bda-363f-880d-cb86dbe27228",
                                        "entry_id": "b528b133-4a9d-3a45-9e61-57d9a5003d46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Catachresis for kilowatt-hour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
